 "6d011bae-a4d7-529c-a458-c67d8283f882" :question/math-academy-id "q-70108" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=3\\cdot 5=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a88f6712-2115-55ce-abe4-b3c27e2e105f" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe556f0-fdf0-5d68-a679-6f5d71362234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386317} {:answer/id #uuid "1489e590-5cb0-507c-9dd8-411b91ddf4ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386318} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9fbfb4-34c8-5ddc-8997-8d9a894af164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386319} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae0cd4e-0b75-583e-bfe0-716308d9c280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386320} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae2a922-02b7-5e56-b372-eea9b6989f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ae0cd4e-0b75-583e-bfe0-716308d9c280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386320} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce784a01-8d71-5a4f-9f59-08e4e36d7ee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfa05fc0-6063-57b8-9b97-f3cee2bfee26" :question/math-academy-id "q-77481" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "The $3$rd row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{31}+3\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+0\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56f22b1b-56ec-56cf-a95e-5764d1146eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327610} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7816e1-4437-5c8a-8e4f-c1ac979ada06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327611} {:answer/id #uuid "3ecc7125-e905-5796-abd2-9afb369f573a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327612} {:answer/id #uuid "abc9b6ec-4646-5be6-bd8a-6994a148b4dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327613} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7fa3eb-3f42-57a7-8880-dcf490a09f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56f22b1b-56ec-56cf-a95e-5764d1146eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327610} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0be2271-17db-5bcd-b673-c40529ab18db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34815fa8-ef8e-5e0c-9946-fa850b2969e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-77487" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{21}+5\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-0)+5(-6-4) \\\\  & =3-50 \\\\  & =-47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+5\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-2)-5(-8-4) \\\\  & =-2+60 \\\\  & =58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-47+58=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053ce7a7-e30d-5fc9-838b-2e9e0898f2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309873} {:answer/id #uuid "294f0a9c-7038-57e2-8764-ffc9d9a19df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309874} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f051ba-97df-5697-9e45-45b3137ebdd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309875} {:answer/id #uuid "f83d9a05-a308-5783-9f85-e867b9f87606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309876} {:answer/id #uuid "24b833f3-1a50-5a60-9f6c-d9dcf0f861fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f051ba-97df-5697-9e45-45b3137ebdd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309875} :answer-field/id #uuid "45dde8a7-0c5c-54a0-bdff-4598f2273f14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ec0fb73-379b-5a1f-918f-29c718e49441" :question/math-academy-id "q-77501" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot {C}_{43} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-1)^{4+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c281252-9a71-5e69-8454-fafa0dd17db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0.2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309880} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f75534-c9e9-5d1d-9eb4-f94d5308ecbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|+0.3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309881} {:answer/id #uuid "08f10a97-f731-5397-8393-ca9d5b9d25c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0.5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309882} {:answer/id #uuid "c936df29-c253-5dea-9f07-9fb2554004e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309883} {:answer/id #uuid "064c835e-19e9-5913-97de-9d3633637da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0.2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "064c835e-19e9-5913-97de-9d3633637da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0.2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309884} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad710733-e7b1-557e-95ee-435ea31675c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "963a5774-5467-51bd-ac21-b66f9097c5fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-77506" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0.5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0.5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0.5\\cdot {C}_{22}+0.2\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|+0.2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|-0.2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1595ed-d8f5-552e-8664-20f16fd916f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386324} {:answer/id #uuid "a430bcc2-9907-54ec-8a56-cc5eeed5f638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386325} {:answer/id #uuid "36d3a662-6530-5790-a658-73b6b5bea937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386326} {:answer/id #uuid "05559a09-9dd8-5cb5-ad32-0e96d722521f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386327} {:answer/id #uuid "f52a1fb8-5907-5281-9da6-7cdfbd4271cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05559a09-9dd8-5cb5-ad32-0e96d722521f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386327} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce55b07-8fc2-5678-b9fa-9bc66f752c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc2737ad-9661-5058-a34f-99a5440f4b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-77800" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+3\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7-0 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=3(-7)=-21.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e1c48a-a17c-503f-9bcb-2f4956fc6ac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386331} {:answer/id #uuid "b67dfd61-89c0-54f9-977c-2c60f5dd11bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386332} {:answer/id #uuid "979174bf-18d7-5b7a-ab0f-c6e68bc4a137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386333} {:answer/id #uuid "753f6780-0984-554b-9b23-69e36a0c9027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386334} {:answer/id #uuid "9478810b-076e-5574-b2b8-e913ee91e5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9478810b-076e-5574-b2b8-e913ee91e5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386335} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f6ccf54-98d1-58f4-b577-8321d09bf3d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f62396c6-1691-5457-8833-10a94ba78d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-77802" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =-2\\cdot {C}_{41}+5\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+0\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{11}+1\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-7)-(-8+2) \\\\  & =11+6 \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+1\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4-7)-(0+0) \\\\  & =-11-0 \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|=2(17)+5(-11)=-21.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50b9fcb0-8034-52ce-9cda-328a7d3c908d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386338} {:answ